  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A meter bridge setup is shown in the figure. It is used to determine an unknown resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;using a given resistor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The galvanometer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>G</mi></mfenced></math> shows null defection when tapping key is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>43</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> mark from end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. If the end correction for end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, then the determined value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0163_7b520068b538.png\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 177px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "19",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using the conditions of a balanced wheatstone bridge and adding the end correction.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>43</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>102</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>45</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>57</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p>"
  }
}